-- gearinfo/res/Odyssey_augments.lua
-- Per-rank augment tables for RP-rank-augmented equipment — primarily
-- Odyssey Sheol: Gaol rewards across all Atonement tiers:
--   * the six armor sets (Nyame, Sakpata, Gleti, Mpaca, Ikenga, Agwu),
--     including every augment path a set offers (each path is its own
--     entry — e.g. Nyame Helm Path A = [438], Path B = [443]),
--   * the Gaol weapons (e.g. Ikenga's Axe = [397]),
--   * Atonement 1/2 equipment with lower rank caps (the item's own
--     max rank — 15/20/25/30 — is read from its exdata, so caps need
--     no special handling here),
-- plus any other gear sharing the same client "bundle" augment
-- encoding (extdata augment_system 4, AugmentSubKind 0x83).
--
-- Format (differs from DREMA_Augments.lua by design): entries are NOT
-- keyed by item id. The item's exdata stores an AugmentIndex (uint32
-- at exdata bytes 9..12, little-endian) naming one entry below, plus
-- the current Rank (0..30) and max-rank tier — so resolution reads
-- everything from the item itself and never guesses. Each entry is a
-- list of effects:
--     { { fmt1 [, fmt2 ...] }, { v0, v1, ... v30 } }
-- where vN is the effect value at rank N (lua index = rank + 1) and
-- each fmt is a string.format pattern producing the in-game augment
-- line (multi-stat effects carry one format per stat, sharing the
-- value). A value of 0 means the effect is inactive at that rank.
--
-- Generated mechanically from LandSandBoat's scripts/data/augments.lua
-- (xi.data.augments.bundles — parsed from FFXI client data; GPL-3.0,
-- https://github.com/LandSandBoat/server), with display formatting
-- derived from the client DAT format strings. Verified against
-- bg-wiki rank breakdown tables (bundle 408 = Ikenga's Hat Path A,
-- all 30 ranks) and set-page max augments for Nyame paths A/B and
-- Ikenga's Axe.
--
-- DO NOT hand-edit values; regenerate from source if SE changes data.

